From d54c4d15a8a5712c9799d25cd5a879eb38f9164e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 22:56:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 181/209] feat(area): polygon point tool - insert, delete,
 drag, snap

CShapeEditTool now reproduces EditorQt's CEditShapeTool (ShapeObject.cpp:62-470)
gesture for gesture, through IShapeComponentEdit alone, so one tool serves every
shape kind and the box's two-corner resize keeps working unchanged:

- click a point to select it (the handle highlights), click away to deselect;
- drag it freely with the mouse on the construction plane, with grid snapping
  and terrain riding when snap-to-terrain is on, or on an axis with the
  transform manipulator - both paths exist in legacy and both are here;
- Ctrl+click on an edge inserts a point there; the edge under the cursor is
  highlighted while Ctrl is held, and on the closing edge the point is appended
  rather than inserted before point 0 ("if last edge, insert at end", :302);
- double-click on a point, or Delete with one selected, removes it; the
  component refuses to drop a closed polygon below three points and warns, and
  the tool then leaves no empty undo step behind;
- Ctrl+Shift+click snaps the selected point onto terrain or geometry through
  rwi_stop_at_pierceable, the legacy call (:440-469);
- Esc leaves the tool.

One CUndo per gesture (insert and remove are one step each), each followed by
the snapshot sync a viewport edit has to perform by hand. The hull is drawn from
GetContour with the new IsContourClosed() flag, so an open polygon no longer
draws a closing edge that is not there.

The resolve-from-GUID and sync helpers both tools need moved into
Tools/ShapeToolCommon.{h,cpp}; no STL container crosses the plugin boundary
anywhere - points are read into stack buffers (heap rule, IShapeComponent.h).

